    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186133828,
      "id": "16a9183a-68b4-5bad-b2d8-3bcf6597f263",
      "title": "Evaluating Line Integrals of a Vector-Valued Functions Over Plane Curves"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b49470dd-5a87-5cb0-85c0-be310dfd4be6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(- y - 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- x + y)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(- t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- 2 t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm d \\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- t + 1,\\quad y=- 2 t + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- y - 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- x + y)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- \\left(- 2 t + 1\\right) - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +\\left(- \\left(- t + 1\\right) + \\left(- 2 t + 1\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(2 t - 2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- t)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(-1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-2)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(2 t - 2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- t)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(-1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-2)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(2 t - 2)\\cdot(-1)+(- t)\\cdot(-2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 2 t + 2}\\right)+\\left({2 t}\\right) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{2 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((2))-((0)) \\\\ &=(2)-(0) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
