    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ed638753-d386-51dc-b401-2a5d2fa865be",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(y + 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(x - y + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(- t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t - 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm d \\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- t,\\quad y=2 t - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(y + 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(x - y + 1)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(\\left(2 t - 1\\right) + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +\\left(\\left(- t\\right) - \\left(2 t - 1\\right) + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- 3 t + 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 1)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(-1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- 3 t + 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(-1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(2 t)\\cdot(-1)+(- 3 t + 2)\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\left({- 2 t}\\right)+\\left({- 6 t + 4}\\right) \\\\ &=- 8 t + 4\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 8 t + 4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- 4 t^{2} + 4 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-4)+(4))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(0)-(0) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
