    "question": {
      ":question/id": "25b796e6-8fb9-5f66-be16-4fcaf972aea8",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(y - 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(x - 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- t - 2)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,1].$\n\n*Hint:* Use $\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\mathrm d \\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\mathrm dt$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t + 1,\\quad y=- t - 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(y - 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(x - 2)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(- t - 2\\right) - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\left(\\left(t + 1\\right) - 2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(- t - 3)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t - 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t + 1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 2)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-1)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({(- t - 3)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t - 1)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({(1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(-1)\\,\\mathbf{j}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=(- t - 3)\\cdot(1)+(t - 1)\\cdot(-1) \\\\ &=\\left({- t - 3}\\right)+\\left({- t + 1}\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 t - 2\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left({- 2 t - 2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- t^{2} - 2 t}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=((-1)+(-2))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(-3)-(0) \\\\ &=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
